  "rationale": "At a comma after an introductory phrase, the model assigns most probability to <END> (0.88) instead of the proper-noun subject observed across the batch. The existing high-weight <END> rule for any final punctuation is too broad: reduce it while retaining the separate strong rule for explicit story-ending forms. Add moderate evidence for each available proper-name token after a terminal comma, capturing the reusable subject-after-introductory-comma pattern rather than one name. Commas can also occur in lists or other constructions where a name is not next, so alternatives remain possible. The free-generation sample is diagnostic, not training evidence. These changes are provisional and have not passed replay or acceptance gates.",
